BT 1 0 0 1 72 684 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (Alder Grange was built in 1897 for the Vane family and passed to the trust in 1974. The estate comprises) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 671.5 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (the main house, two cotenanted lodges, a walled garden, and forty-one rooms of varying condition across) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 659 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (three floors. The trust has maintained the roof and services on an annual cycle, but no major restoration) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 646.5 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (has been undertaken since 1998.) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 626 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (The 2027 programme responds to two pressures. Rainwater goods and roof coverings have reached the) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 613.5 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (end of their service life, and the trust has committed to opening the east wing to visitors by the summer of) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 601 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (2029, which requires fire and access works that cannot be deferred.) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 576.5 Tm /F2 12 Tf 14.4 TL (Section 2: Condition survey) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 556.5 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (The condition survey was carried out in November 2026 over eleven survey days and covered all) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 544 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (forty-one rooms together with the roof voids. The survey found the roof coverings generally sound but the) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 531.5 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (lead flashings at the end of their life, and found localised timber decay in the east wing where gutters) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 519 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (have overflowed.) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 498.5 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (The survey report runs to ninety pages and is summarised here. Its central finding, as detailed in Section) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 486 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (3 \(page 3\), is that the roof programme dominates the cost plan and should be sequenced before any) Tj ET
BT 1 0 0 1 72 473.5 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL (internal works.) Tj ET
 

